                <pb facs="0822" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg688"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 643.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir T. V. Lister to
                        Mr. Phelps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 16,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to thank you for your
                    letter of the 12th instant, informing me that Mr. Henry White, first secretary
                    of the United States legation at this court, has been authorized by the United
                    States Government to attend the sugar conference in a friendly way.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. V.
                        Lister.</hi></signed><lb/>(For the Marquis of
                    Salisbury.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
